WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.330
Apple Silicon systems can run local chat interfaces, web UIs, local inference APIs,

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:08.536
coding tools, document workflows, and private assistants.

00:00:08.536 --> 00:00:10.655
Once a local model is served through an endpoint,

00:00:10.655 --> 00:00:13.110
it can become part of a broader application workflow.

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.680
That is useful, but it also changes the risk profile.

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.185
The model is no longer only an interactive experiment.

00:00:18.185 --> 00:00:19.886
It is a service other tools may call.

00:00:19.886 --> 00:00:24.230
Localhost binding is a safer default for private inference services because it limits

00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:25.640
access to the local machine.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:29.580
LAN access can be useful for a homelab or team environment, but it should be deliberate.

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:31.730
Reverse proxies, authentication, TLS,

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:36.250
and access policy may be needed at a high level if other users or devices connect.

00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:40.235
Avoid accidental exposure of a local model endpoint to untrusted networks.

00:00:40.235 --> 00:00:43.315
Applications that call local models should be scoped carefully.

00:00:43.315 --> 00:00:47.490
A coding tool, document assistant, or private chat interface may send sensitive prompts,

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.840
files, or context to the inference endpoint.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:00:52.160
If several applications share one local service,

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:55.530
operators should understand which data flows through it, whether logs are retained,

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.960
and whether different workflows should be separated.

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.690
Serving local models is not just a convenience feature.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:05.070
It requires decisions about access control, logging, retention, uptime, update timing,

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:06.200
and failure behavior.

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:09.120
Treat prompts and outputs as potentially sensitive data.

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.040
Local inference can improve privacy,

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:15.665
but only when service exposure and surrounding application behavior are managed with

00:01:15.665 --> 00:01:15.680
intention.
